WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:07.490
Real games feel real because things fall like they do in the real world. Today you’ll code gravity!

2
00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:11.650
Make a variable called vy (velocity in y).

3
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:16.140
It says how many steps the sprite moves up or down each frame.

4
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.620
Negative vy means falling.

5
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:25.440
Every frame, gravity changes vy by -1, then the sprite changes y by vy.

6
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.900
The fall gets faster and faster — just like a real apple.

7
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:37.100
If the sprite goes below the floor, put it back on the floor and set vy to 0 so it stops falling.

8
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:41.430
In another forever loop, check the arrow keys and change x.

9
00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:45.180
Now the hero can walk and fall at the same time.

10
00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:49.080
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

11
00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:53.800
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
